dev (b2a4bda3b) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-14500 (20 threads) - 31.77 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using terrain sets with `TileMapLayer` and you erase cells while using \"Match Corners\" mode, not all neighbours of the erased cell are updated, only the diagonal cells are updated.\n\nCells that share a side with the erased cell should be updated.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn my test scenario, my terrain is setup like so:\n\n<img width=\"301\" height=\"292\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e27ed225-b47e-48cf-86a2-109233023a28\" />\n\nif I draw this with the rectangle tool then erase 2 cells...\n\n<img width=\"213\" height=\"211\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8adba6cf-9c77-46fc-a1bd-3ae3886833e4\" />\n\nThis is what happens currently\n\n<img width=\"198\" height=\"201\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/517e0c4b-a630-4b7b-b8d5-1a279b2bc6d1\" />\n\nThe expected outcome should be something like this\n\n<img width=\"210\" height=\"208\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ce09c69-d421-4352-85ae-556598e879ed\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[cell erase issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23205415/cell.erase.issue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api